Rick Harrison posted this on Usenet alt.languages.artificial
> Where is a good place (is there a good place) to post questions about
> "how do you say ___ in Lojban" and "how do you say ___ in Volapük"? 
> 
> I am resuming work on a multilingual dictionary project, so this won't
> be just one or two questions per lifetime... it will be a steady
> trickle of questions.
> 
> At the moment I'm looking for the names of two moon phases, called
> 
> "full moon" and "new moon" in English... 
> 
> "luna yen" and "luna nobo" in Papiamentu...
> 
> "mwezi mpevu" and "mwezi mchanga" in Swahili.

I suggested that he post to Lojban list or visit the IRC channel, but if 
someone else wants to monitor that Usenet newsgroup who likes to answer 
such questions, I encourage you to let him know that you are doing so.

I could coin a bunch of possible tanru or lujvo for these two concepts, 
but I cannot claim that any of them are better/more correct than others. 
  Maybe someone else has stronger feelings.

